# <type>(<optional scope>): <description>
#   |<----  use the imperative, present tense: "add", not "added"  ---->|
#   |<----  keep the whole subject line under 72 characters        ---->|

# Why is this change needed, and what does it do? Wrap at 72 columns.

# Footers: breaking changes and issue references.
# BREAKING CHANGE: <what broke and what to do instead>
#   PRs are squash-merged, so repeat this footer in the PR description — that
#   description becomes the commit body release-please reads.
# Refs: #123
# Closes: #123

# type must be one of:
#   feat     a new user-facing capability          (minor version bump)
#   fix      a bug fix                             (patch version bump)
#   perf     a performance improvement
#   refactor a change that is neither a fix nor a feature
#   docs     documentation only
#   test     tests only
#   style    formatting only, no behaviour change
#   build    build system or dependencies
#   ci       CI configuration
#   chore    anything else that does not touch src/
#   revert   reverts a previous commit
#
# A `!` after the type/scope, or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer, marks a breaking
# change. The squash discards branch subjects, so the `!` has to be in the PR
# title too. If it changes the extension contract in a way that is not purely
# additive, raise the CONTRACT_VERSION question in the PR — when to bump is not
# a settled rule. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# This template is a local convenience and is NOT enforced. The commit-msg
# commitlint hook is the actual gate.
